1.What is Ensemble Learning in Machine Learning?
Ensemble learning is a machine learning technique where multiple models(weak learners) are trained and combined
to solve the same problem in order to get better accuracy,stability and robustness.

2.Why do we use multiple models instead of relying on a single Machine Learning model?
A single model may overfiy or underfit the data. Different model capture different patterns, combining them helps
balance bias and variance. Ensembles are more robust and generalize better to unseen data.

3.What is meant by a base learner or base estimator?
A base learner is an individual model that contributes to the ensemble.
Eg Decision Tree, Logistic Regression,
Each base learner makes predications and the ensemble combine them (averaging or voting).


4.What is the main idea behind Ensemble Learning?
The main idea is "wisdom of the crowd"
Just as a group of people can make better decisions collectively, multiple models can produce more accurate
predications together than one model alone.

5.What are the major types of Ensemble Learning techniques?
Bagging (Bootstrap Aggregating)
Boosting
Voting

6.Explain the difference between:
Bagging - Train multiple models independently on random subsets of the data and average/vote their predications.
          Reduce variance, avoids overfitting, works well with unstable models
          Useful in spam detection, credit scoring.

Boosting - Train models sequentially where each models learns from the mistakes of the previous ones.
          Useful in customer churn prediction, fraud detection.

Voting - Combines predications from different models (Hard - 1/0, Soft- gives in probability)

7.Can Ensemble Learning be used for both classification and regression? Explain with examples.
Yes,
Classification - Random Forest Classifier, AdaBoost Classifier
Regression - Random Forest Regressor,Gradient Boosting Regressor
Both cases, ensembles aggregate predications(majority vote for classification, average for regression)

8.Why is diversity among models important in an ensemble?
If all models makes similar errors, combining them won't help.
Diversity ensures that different models capture different aspect od the data, so their errors cancel out- leading better performance.

9.Is combining many models always better than using a single model? Justify your answer.
Not always,
If models are too similar, the ensemble add little value.
If model are too complex,it may increase computation and risk overfitting.
Effective ensembles requires diverse and well trained base learners.

10.What are the advantages and disadvantages of Ensemble Learning?

Advantages	                    Disadvantages
Higher accuracy and robustness	Increased computational cost
Reduces overfitting and variance	Harder to interpret
Works well for complex problems	Requires careful tuning and diversity
